[Music]  but first thousands of supporters of  pakistan's former prime minister imran  khan are gathering in the city of lahore  they're expecting to hold a mass protest  in the coming hours khan is pushing for  a return to power after losing a  no-confidence vote in april kamal haider  is joining us live from lahore so what  is the significance of the rally taking  place today  is hugely significant given the fact  that imran khan's government was thrown  out  through a word of no confidence not just  in islamabad but here in the punjab  province also  however there was a run-off election  his party is now back in power  and this is of course his first major  rally  in the provincial capital  of the province now it is also  significant because pakistan is  celebrating  its 75th independence day tomorrow  and this is the eve of  pakistan's independence which is also  pakistan's diamond jubilee so indeed he  wants to send a message  and he of course will be announcing his  next line of action because he and his  supporters have been demanding an early  election saying that the country needs a  fresh mandate and without that the  country cannot come out of the huge  economic crisis that pakistan is  confronted with okay thank you so much  kamal haider reporting for us from  lahore

